at 32x256 the kernel work is trivial and the cost is almost entirely per-op
launch + Python dispatch (4 launches per call).  For an input signature that
repeats (same buffers, shape, stride, dtype, device) the four elementwise
kernels are recorded once into a CUDA graph and afterwards re-issued with a
single graph launch, removing 3 of 4 launches and most of the dispatch cost.
The graph reads the caller's live input buffers, so a replay always reflects
the current input contents; the static graph output is cloned before being
