    #   1) out   = x * 1.25            (out-of-place, allocates)
    #   2) out  += 0.75 * y            (add_ with alpha, no temporary)
    #   3) out  -= 0.125
    #   4) out   = max(out, 0)         (in-place relu, returns the same buffer)
    # Folding 0.75 into add_'s alpha removes the separate y*0.75 multiply; the
    # only numeric effect is that alpha*b may be contracted with the add (<=0.5
    # ulp on values <= 10, i.e. ~1e-6), far inside atol/rtol = 1e-5.
